{"text": "IN THE SUPERIOR COURT OF THE STATE OF ARIZONA\nIN AND FOR THE COUNTY OF PIMA\n\nLEOCADIA M. WAWRZYNIAK, a married woman,\n            Plaintiff,\nvs.                                             No. C20254417\nGREENMANTLE GROCERS, INC., an Arizona corporation; JOHN DOES 1-5,\n            Defendants.\n\nDEPOSITION OF LEOCADIA WAWRZYNIAK\nTucson, Arizona\nOctober 9, 2025, 9:32 a.m.\n\nAPPEARANCES\nFor the Plaintiff:   Rashida N. Holcombe, Esq., Holcombe & Ilves, PLLC\n                     2210 E. Speedway Blvd., Suite 140, Tucson, AZ 85719\n                     rholcombe@holcombeilves.example\nFor the Defendant:   Garrett T. Ulbricht, Esq., Dunmow Pryce LLP\n                     One South Church Avenue, 18th Floor, Tucson, AZ 85701\nAlso present:        Zbigniew Wawrzyniak\nReported by:         Paulette Dzialo, RPR, Certified Reporter No. 50844\n\n                                                                 Page 6\nEXAMINATION BY MR. ULBRICHT:\n Q.  Good morning, ma'am. Would you state your full name for the record?\n A.  Leocadia Maria Wawrzyniak. Everybody calls me Lottie.\n Q.  Have you ever gone by any other name?\n A.  My maiden name was Stachura.\n Q.  And your date of birth?\n A.  March 3rd, 1958.\n Q.  Where do you live currently?\n A.  3391 North Calle Zaragoza, here in Tucson. We've been there since about two thousand eleven.\n Q.  Who lives there with you?\n A.  Just my husband, Ziggy. Zbigniew. He's sitting right there.\n Q.  I don't want your whole Social Security number on the record, just the last four digits.\n     MS. HOLCOMBE:  Last four only, Lottie.\n A.  4570.\n Q.  Is there a phone number where you can be reached if we need to reschedule anything?\n A.  My cell is five two zero, five five five, zero one four seven. Or email, it's lottie.w58@sonoramail.example.\n\n                                                                 Page 9\n Q.  Where were you working in the spring of this year?\n A.  I worked the front desk at Tortolita Family Dental. I'd been there six years.\n Q.  What were you earning?\n A.  Nineteen dollars an hour, thirty-two hours a week most weeks.\n Q.  Let's talk about the day of the incident. What day was it?\n A.  It was the Saturday before Easter. April 19th.\n Q.  And which store were you in?\n A.  The Greenmantle on Oracle Road, the one by the car wash. I shop there every week.\n Q.  What time did you arrive?\n A.  A little after ten in the morning. I remember because I had just dropped Ziggy at the union hall.\n Q.  Which union hall is that?\n A.  He's with the Sheet Metal Workers, Local 359. Our health insurance comes through them.\n Q.  Tell me what happened once you were inside.\n A.  I got a cart, I went to produce first like I always do. I wanted grapes. There is a display on the end, and when\n     I came around it my right foot just went out from under me. I went down on my left side, hard.\n Q.  Did you see anything on the floor before you fell?\n A.  No. After, when I was lying there, I could see water and some crushed grapes, and a long skid mark from my shoe.\n Q.  Was there a cone or a wet floor sign anywhere in that aisle?\n A.  Not that I saw. Not until afterwards, when a boy in an apron brought one over.\n Q.  What kind of shoes were you wearing?\n A.  Sneakers. The white ones I wear to work. They were maybe three months old.\n Q.  Did anyone come to help you?\n A.  A young woman with a toddler in her cart. She stayed with me the whole time and she called 911. She told me her name\n     was Marisol Tsinajinnie. She said she works at the university bookstore. I wrote her number on my hand.\n Q.  Did you speak with anyone from the store?\n A.  The manager came. Nacho. I think his real name is Ignacio. Barrientos.\n Q.  What did Mr. Barrientos say to you?\n A.  He said, \"I told them twice already this morning to mop that up.\" Those were his words. Then he asked me to sign\n     a paper, and I said I can't sign anything, look at my hand.\n Q.  I'm showing you what has been marked Exhibit 4. Is that the paper?\n A.  I think so. It says incident report IR-114-0419-02 at the top. That is not my signature at the bottom.\n\n                                                                 Page 14\n Q.  How did you leave the store?\n A.  By ambulance. They took me to Rincon Vista Medical Center.\n Q.  What were you told about your injuries?\n A.  That I had a broken left wrist and a hairline fracture in my hip.\n Q.  Did you have surgery?\n A.  Dr. Kelkar put a plate and screws in the wrist on the 22nd. The hip they left alone, but I was on a walker\n     for seven weeks.\n Q.  Before this fall, had you ever injured that wrist or that hip?\n A.  No.\n Q.  Do you have any ongoing medical conditions?\n A.  I've had type 2 diabetes since my forties. I take metformin for that. And they told me in 2019 I have osteoporosis.\n Q.  Who told you that?\n A.  My regular doctor, after a bone scan.\n     MS. HOLCOMBE:  Objection to the extent this calls for a medical opinion. You can answer what you know.\n Q.  Have you ever been a party to a lawsuit before this one?\n A.  No. Well. We filed a bankruptcy, a Chapter 13, back in 2012. I don't know if that counts.\n Q.  Was that discharged?\n A.  Yes. We paid for five years.\n Q.  When did you go back to work?\n A.  June 30. Part time at first. I still can't type the way I used to.\n Q.  Let me show you Exhibit 7. Do you recognize it?\n A.  It's the hospital bill. Forty-one thousand and change.\n Q.  The total shown is $41,286.90. Has any part of that been paid, to your knowledge?\n A.  The union plan paid some. We got a letter that they want it back out of the case.\n     MR. ULBRICHT:  Let's take ten minutes.\n     (Recess taken from 10:51 a.m. to 11:04 a.m.)\n\n                                                                 Page 31\n     (Deposition concluded at 12:17 p.m. Signature reserved under Rule 30(e).)\n\nREPORTER'S CERTIFICATE\nI, Paulette Dzialo, certify that the foregoing pages are a true record of the testimony given.\nDated October 21, 2025.  Job No. 25-10-0933", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "1,011 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Leocadia M. WAWRZYNIAK", "Rashida N. Holcombe", "Garrett T. Ulbricht", "Zbigniew Wawrzyniak", "Marisol Tsinajinnie", "Dr. Kelkar"], "companies": ["GREENMANTLE GROCERS, INC.", "Holcombe & Ilves, PLLC", "Dunmow Pryce LLP", "Tortolita Family Dental", "Greenmantle", "Sheet Metal Workers", "Local 359", "University Bookstore", "Rincon Vista Medical Center", "Union plan"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Tucson", "Arizona", "Tortolita Family Dental", "Greenmantle", "Oracle Road", "union hall", "university bookstore"], "health": ["fall", "water", "crushed grapes", "skid mark", "sneakers", "diabetes", "type 2 diabetes", "metformin", "osteoporosis"], "sensitive": [], "names": ["Leocadia", "Maria", "Lottie", "Zbigniew", "Ziggy", "Marisol", "Nacho", "Ignacio"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 3, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 7.399999998509884, "modelMs": 36480.39999999851, "topicMs": 40322.30000000447, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 38, "end": 45, "text": "ARIZONA", "kind": "region", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "ARIZONA"}, {"start": 77, "end": 99, "text": "LEOCADIA M. WAWRZYNIAK", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Leocadia Maria Wawrzyniak"}, {"start": 193, "end": 202, "text": "C20254417", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "C20254417"}, {"start": 203, "end": 228, "text": "GREENMANTLE GROCERS, INC.", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "GREENMANTLE GROCERS, IN